  (text "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 PIN MAP — keep firmware (components/dbcan, net, bridge) in step.\n\n  USB      D+ = IO20, D- = IO19   FIXED IN SILICON, not reassignable.\n                                  The symbol names them USB_D+/USB_D-.\n  TWAI/CAN CAN_TX = IO4, CAN_RX = IO5      -> ADM3053 on the dbCAN sheet\n  W5500    SCK=IO12  MOSI=IO11  MISO=IO13\n           CSn=IO10  INTn=IO14   RSTn=IO9  -> Ethernet sheet\n  LEDs     LAN=IO15  ERR=IO16  CAN=IO17    (active HIGH, 1k series)\n  PD       PD_PG=IO18 (CH224K power-good, open-drain active LOW)\n  Straps   BOOT=IO0 (SW302), EN=reset (SW301 + R301/C304)\n\nWhy these pins: IO9-IO18 have no strapping function and no flash/PSRAM role, so\nthey are safe for outputs at reset. AVOIDED: IO0/IO3/IO45/IO46 are strapping pins;\nIO26-IO32 are the module's internal SPI flash and are not brought out; IO35-IO37\nare used by octal-PSRAM variants, so leaving them free keeps a -N8R8 module a\ndrop-in option later.\n\nJ301 IS A RECOVERY PATH, NOT A CONVENIENCE.\nProgramming now runs over native USB-CDC, so a USB stack that fails to enumerate\nwould otherwise leave no way in. J301 exposes UART0 + BOOT + EN so the module can\nalways be flashed by the ROM bootloader over serial. 1.27mm pitch to keep it small;\nit is a bring-up/service header, not a user port.\n\nUnused GPIOs are flagged no-connect deliberately, so a spare pin is visibly spare\nrather than an oversight."
    (at 40 135 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)))
    (uuid "0c4a1853-a70f-4a8b-ab75-453ad113978d"))

